<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 5 February, from 62 to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">62 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,964 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake strikes Pompeii and Herculaneum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A strong earthquake badly damaged towns around the Bay of Naples. Pompeii was still being repaired seventeen years later when Vesuvius buried it in 79.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1597 CE <span class="tih-ago">429 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Twenty-six Christians crucified at Nagasaki</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the orders of Toyotomi Hideyoshi, six Franciscan missionaries, Japanese Jesuits and lay converts were crucified on a hill at Nagasaki. They are honoured as the Twenty-Six Martyrs of Japan.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1783 CE <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Calabrian earthquakes begin in southern Italy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first of five major shocks struck Calabria and Sicily, beginning a sequence that lasted weeks. Around 30,000 to 50,000 people died, and the disaster prompted early scientific study of earthquakes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1852 CE <span class="tih-ago">174 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Hermitage museum opens to the public in St Petersburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nicholas I opened the purpose-built New Hermitage to display the imperial art collections. The Hermitage is now one of the largest museums in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1900 CE <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and the United States sign the first Hay-Pauncefote Treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The agreement gave the United States the right to build a canal across Central America. Rejected by the Senate, it was renegotiated in 1901, opening the way for the Panama Canal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1924 CE <span class="tih-ago">102 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">BBC broadcasts the Greenwich time signal for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The six short 'pips', generated by the Royal Observatory at Greenwich, were broadcast to mark the hour. The signal is still heard on BBC radio today.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1971 CE <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 14 lands at Fra Mauro</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alan Shepard and Edgar Mitchell landed in the lunar highlands, the target of the aborted Apollo 13. Shepard, America's first astronaut in space, became the fifth person to walk on the Moon.</p></div></li></ol>
